  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let \\(f(x)=x^2+3x+2\\) and let \\(S\\) be the set of integers \\(\\{0,1,2,\\ldots,25\\}.\\) The number of members \\(s\\) of \\(S\\) such that \\(f(s)\\) has remainder zero when divided by \\(6\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(25\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(22\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(21\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(18\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(17\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "17"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\(f(s)=(s+1)(s+2),\\) a product of consecutive integers, so it is always even. It is divisible by \\(3\\) unless \\(s\\equiv0\\pmod3.\\) Among \\(0,1,\\ldots,25,\\) nine values are multiples of \\(3.\\) Thus \\(26-9=17\\) values work.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\(f(s)\\) as \\((s+1)(s+2)\\)",
        "The product is always even; determine which residue of \\(s\\) modulo \\(3\\) fails"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
